The earlier attempts show that collisions in the coefficient sum are what fail, except the `t4`/`t6` pair, which passed in attempt 3. This version uses `t7 = 2·t5·t2 − t3`, which sits at level 7 on its own. The only same-level pair is then `t4`/`t6`, and `t5` has level 6 to itself. All subtractions involve operands at different levels.

